<h1>The SNOT Troubleshooting Strategy</h1>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px;">
<p>📖 <b>Troubleshooting</b> is a form of problem-solving that involves using a logical and systematic search for the source of a problem.</p>
</div>
<br>

<p>The SNOT Strategy provides a structured approach for troubleshooting problems, helping students develop independence and critical thinking skills when faced with challenges.</p>

<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px; max-width: 900px; margin: 20px auto;">

  <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 15px;">
    <div style="width: 60px; height: 60px; border-radius: 50%; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; font-size: 24px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; flex-shrink: 0;">S</div>
    <div style="flex: 1; background-color: #F7F7FB; padding: 15px; border-radius: 10px;">
      <h3>Step 1: Self</h3>
      <p>Restate the problem and make your best guesses about possible solutions.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 15px;">
    <div style="width: 60px; height: 60px; border-radius: 50%; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; font-size: 24px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; flex-shrink: 0;">N</div>
    <div style="flex: 1; background-color: #F7F7FB; padding: 15px; border-radius: 10px;">
      <h3>Step 2: Neighbor</h3>
      <p>Talk through the problem with someone to share viewpoints and narrow down possibilities.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 15px;">
    <div style="width: 60px; height: 60px; border-radius: 50%; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; font-size: 24px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; flex-shrink: 0;">O</div>
    <div style="flex: 1; background-color: #F7F7FB; padding: 15px; border-radius: 10px;">
      <h3>Step 3: Online Resources</h3>
      <p>Search message boards, technical manuals, FAQs, and other online resources to further narrow down possible solutions.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 15px;">
    <div style="width: 60px; height: 60px; border-radius: 50%; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; font-size: 24px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; flex-shrink: 0;">T</div>
    <div style="flex: 1; background-color: #F7F7FB; padding: 15px; border-radius: 10px;">
      <h3>Step 4: Technical Expert</h3>
      <p>Ask a technical or subject-matter expert who can provide guidance.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>

<div style="background-color: #E4E2F8; color: #222222; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 20px 0;">
<p><strong>💡 Teacher tip:</strong> having a clear troubleshooting strategy like SNOT encourages students to become problem-solvers instead of immediately seeking help. It builds resilience, promotes collaboration, and teaches them how to find and evaluate reliable resources, an essential skill for coding, data science, and beyond.</p>
</div>

<h2>Let's Try a Troubleshooting Activity</h2>
MARKDOWN
